Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-04-2001||02:09 AM||||Sorry to start another topic about the temporary shutdown of the forum, but I wanted to hear some opinions.  I'm getting the impression that some of the members who spend a lot of time on the forum are getting satisfaction from seeing an occasional soap opera(incident) occur on the forum.  I'm thinking that this phenomenon is very similar to the way I apparently enjoy "throwing a wrench into the machine" everytime my life is going smoothly.  Is it intentional or simply an accident? I visit the forum for technical info and comedic value, but it seems that it's gone wayyyyy beyond that for some people.   I've gotten hours of entertainment from poking fun at certain members for obvious stupidity, but it's all in fun.  Why do we need to turn a perfectly innocent forum into real-life? I get enough of that when I'm not online.  I'm sure someone else has probably already said everything that I've just said, but I'm far too lazy to read through every post regaurding this subject.  And what's all this about threatening other forum members?  I've seen this happen among members on more than one occasion, and it's horrifically childish.   If someone came to my door and said, "Hi, I'm REDFIEROFRED from the Forum and you've insulted me, so I decided to come to your house and settle this"  I'd probably laugh until I puked.  challenging races is one thing, but threatening physical harm is poppy-**** (I love that term...)  Uhhh yeah, so anyway.... I need to go alphabetize the contents of my fridge.  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">      <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||5
